Eve L: Heads-up: onboarding sampleapp default concurrency just caused a noisy local failure. 429s then retries piled up and node event loop lagged. Repro attached.

Eve L: Repro steps: run sampleapp (defaults) + 25 parallel clients paginating + calling embed/generate. Using JS SDK v0.9.0.

Diego M: Can you paste the retry code? Usually recursion + immediate retry is the culprit.

Eve L: current snippet: 
```js
async function fetchPage(cursor){
  const slot = await sem.acquire();
  try { return await client.list({cursor, token: await auth.token()}); }
  catch(e){ if(isRetryable(e)) return await fetchPage(cursor); throw e; }
  finally{ slot.release(); }
}
```

Rina S: Yep that recursion ignores the concurrency accounting on retries. Fix: retries need to re-acquire the same semaphore and use exp backoff + jitter. Also ensure token refresh is single-flight.

Diego M: JS SDK already has refresh-single-flight but sampleapp examples for Python and Go still show naive refresh. We should standardize: Config.maxConcurrentSequences (default 12) + refresh promise pattern.

Eve L: Quick mitigation I tested: lower default sem from 100 -> 12 and change retry to an explicit loop that acquires slot each attempt. Eliminates OOM and keeps CPU sane.

Rina S: Implementation sketch to land in sampleapp and SDKs:
1) retry wrapper: while(attempts++){ await sem.acquire(); try{ return await fn(); } finally{ sem.release(); } await sleep(expBackoff + jitter); }
2) auth.getToken caches in-flight refresh promise
3) CLI warns if user sets --concurrency > 64 and not --burst-safe

ci-bot: Created ticket DE-3399: "onboard: retry-queue + client defaults + SDK parity for token refresh" assigned to Diego M, Rina S.

Diego M: I'll open the Go+Py parity PRs today and add Config.MaxConcurrentSequences. Rina can update sampleapp retry loop.

Eve L: Awesome — I'll attach small repro harness and flamegraph to DE-3399. Thanks.
